From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken Smith <ken@design-nex.us>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:35:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] virtual monitors: fixes from the first run on a NyxOS VM

- The dispatchers find a split host by its name: a host is hidden from
  monitor queries, so merge({ monitor = HOST }) said it wasn't split.
- Merge remembers each workspace's region by numbered ID: every region after
  the first names its workspaces 1..N too, so by name the first region's
  workspaces came back on the last one.
- Restore puts each remembered workspace back on its region wherever
  creating the regions left it, and once more when the monitor rule reload
  that creating them schedules has run: that reload's persistent workspace
  pass moves workspaces whose rule names no monitor to the focused region.
- After a split or restore, only persistent workspaces whose rule names a
  monitor are put in place, for the same reason.
- Restore returns focus and the pointer to where they were before the merge:
  the host's mode changes move the pointer to the middle of the screen, and
  with focus following the mouse, focus went with it.
- Only the workspace each monitor shows is visible after a split, restore or
  merge: moving without replacing kept a workspace's visibility, so a region
  drew the windows of a workspace it no longer showed.
- A fresh split shows the host's workspace on the region that now has it and
  the lowest-numbered one on the others, not a new empty workspace.
- Region workspace rules are removed, not just disabled, so splitting and
  restoring doesn't add ten rules each time (CWorkspaceRuleManager::remove).
